messages:
sam: Heads-up — ran into a failure when the mobile client strips Content-Type. Client expects a single JSON object but our endpoint sometimes streams ndjson when header is missing, so JSON.parse blows up. Repro:
```
curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN' \ 
  'https://api.redwood.example/v1/generate?stream=true' \
  -o out.txt  # mobile client removed Content-Type earlier in pipeline
```
out.txt is streaming chunks but mobile code tries to parse as whole JSON.

lina: hmm. Is the server choosing streaming because of the `stream=true` query? Or because no Content-Type implies fallback to streaming endpoint? We shouldn't infer response mode solely from missing header.

mike: we currently use this precedence: explicit `Accept: text/event-stream` or `content-type` influences routed behavior, otherwise `stream=true` toggles streaming. But if Content-Type is absent, downstream routing incorrectly treats request as unstructured and picks ndjson path. Bug.

anna: proposed fix: make server explicit: require either `Accept` or `stream=true` to enable streaming. If both absent and client omits Content-Type, default to `application/json` structured response. Also add a safety toggle `legacy_client_fallback` for canary.

sam: sounds good. Minimal change in header parser to avoid guessing. Example patch idea:
```js
// header handling
const ct = req.headers['content-type'];
const accept = req.headers.accept || '';
const wantsStream = req.query.stream === 'true' || /event-stream|ndjson/.test(accept);
if (!ct) {
  // fallback order: query param -> Accept header -> default structured json
  if (req.query.format === 'ndjson' || wantsStream) {
    // serve streaming
  } else {
    // serve structured application/json
  }
}
```

schema-bot: failing test that surfaced this: `tests/responses/test_missing_content_type.py::test_mobile_legacy_behavior` — expects structured JSON but got ndjson chunks. We should update the test to assert the strict fallback and add a case for `format=ndjson`.

ci-bot: build passed on branch `fix/contenttype-fallback` — 5/6 e2e green, flaky test `streaming/buffered-chunk-size` still failing but not related.

mike: small ask — add telemetry event `response_mode_fallback` with tags: `header_present:false`, `query_format:ndjson|json|none`, `client:mobile-legacy?`. That will help identify real traffic.

lina: plan for rollout:
1) unit tests + one integration test asserting default structured response when Content-Type missing
2) add telemetry
3) land behind feature flag `content_type_fallback_v2`
4) canary to 5% for 24h, watch `response_mode_fallback` and `errors.json_parse`
5) if stable, ramp 25% -> 100%

anna: add a note for SDK teams — mobile SDK should set `Accept: application/json` or send `format=json` param. I'll open a docs PR.

sam: I'll put up the PR with the header parser change, tests, and telemetry. pinging @mike and @lina for reviews. Also adding an integration job that simulates a client that strips headers.

mike: will review today, focus on the header heuristics and UT coverage.

lina: I'll coordinate the canary and update the runbook with the metrics to watch. If we see >0.5% increase in `errors.json_parse` we rollback.

sam: thanks all :thumbsup:
